@coderabbitai Addressed in 928e1b02f (building on 6fdd05a28). The outdated window query is replaced by incremental discovery in `.agents/scripts/opencode-db-archive.sh:1441`: fetch candidate IDs, size only the required prefix, stop at the byte limit, and check the deadline before/after each size query. Discovery remains included in batch timing, and the oversized-first-session exception is preserved. Sizing includes part/message/event/session_message data, session-input prompts, and context-epoch baseline/snapshot payloads, using byte lengths.

Verified: `bash .agents/scripts/tests/test-opencode-db-archive.sh` — 73 passed, 0 failed, including prefix/deadline/oversized-session coverage; ShellCheck on both changed files, `bash -n`, and `git diff --check` passed. Pushed to the PR branch. Unrelated repository TypeScript checking was deferred by the existing push hook to CI because local JavaScript dependencies are absent.

<!-- aidevops:review-thread-response:PRRT_kwDOQSEXLM63NJS0 -->

@coderabbitai Deferred to a later Reclaim phase (#38051, phase 3: decision journal, generation key, CAS), not this PR.

Reclaim is not the lifecycle retirement path. It never calls `prepare_retirement` and emits no `cleanup_authorized`. Removal requires all of the following, each checked at judgement and again right before deletion:

- an independent loss proof (`nothing_to_lose`): clean status including untracked files, and zero commits absent from every remote;
- a registered generation (`owner-not-enrolled` refuses);
- no live registered owner.

With these checks, a tree that is missing creation provenance cannot lose data when it is removed. Provenance would narrow *which* trees are eligible, so it belongs with the generation-keyed decision journal. This scope split matches the brief for #38107.

